# 🚀 NASA Flask App — AWS Deployment

A cloud deployment of the [NASA Demo Flask App](https://github.com/davidrichardharvey/nasa-flask-app), demonstrating a scalable, highly available architecture on AWS using EC2, an Application Load Balancer, and an Auto Scaling Group.

> **Live URL:** [http://se-omar-nasa-flask-app-alb-928656398.eu-west-1.elb.amazonaws.com/](http://se-omar-nasa-flask-app-alb-928656398.eu-west-1.elb.amazonaws.com/)

---

## What the App Does

The app integrates with several NASA public APIs and renders the results as web pages:

| Route | Description |
|---|---|
| `/` | Home page — lists all available endpoints |
| `/apod` | Astronomy Picture of the Day |
| `/neo` | Near-Earth Objects (today's asteroid data) |
| `/earth` | Satellite imagery of Earth |

