## Architecture

```
                        Internet
                           │
                           ▼
              ┌────────────────────────┐
              │  Application Load      │
              │  Balancer (ALB)        │
              │  Port 80               │
              └────────────┬───────────┘
                           │ forwards to port 5000
              ┌────────────┴───────────┐
              │    Target Group        │
              │    Port 5000           │
              └──────┬─────────┬───────┘
                     │         │
           ┌─────────┴──┐  ┌───┴──────────┐
           │  EC2 #1    │  │  EC2 #2      │  ← Auto Scaling Group
           │ (AZ-a)     │  │ (AZ-b)       │    min: 1 / desired: 2 / max: 4
           │            │  │              │
           │  Gunicorn  │  │  Gunicorn    │
           │  :5000     │  │  :5000       │
           │            │  │              │
           │  Flask App │  │  Flask App   │
           └────────────┘  └──────────────┘
```

### AWS Resources Used

| Resource | Name | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| EC2 Instance | `nasa-flask-app` | Base instance used to build the AMI |
| AMI | `nasa-flask-app-ami` | Golden image of the configured instance |
| Launch Template | `nasa-flask-lt` | Reusable config for ASG-launched instances |
| Target Group | `nasa-flask-tg` | Routes ALB traffic to instances on port 5000 |
| Load Balancer | `nasa-flask-alb` | Internet-facing ALB, accepts traffic on port 80 |
| Auto Scaling Group | `nasa-flask-asg` | Maintains desired capacity; scales on CPU |

